<title>USA: Clinton to propose 20 cent/pack cigarette tax rise.</title>
<headline>Clinton to propose 20 cent/pack cigarette tax rise.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton plans on Monday to propose raising cigarette taxes by 20 cents per pack, with the revenues generated placed in a trust fund for children's health care, public health and other programs, a White House official said.</p>
<p>The official, who declined to be identified, said Clinton was scheduled to unveil the proposal as part of a broad discussion of his tax initiatives at 0930 EDT (1330 GMT).</p>
</text>
